# Parity fixtures can be large, so they are gitignored by default and
# un-ignored individually as they are committed.
#
# "Not committed" is NOT the same as "generated on demand" — nothing in CI
# generates them, so an un-committed fixture means that port has no numerical
# parity coverage at all. That gap is declared explicitly in PARITY_COVERAGE
# (tests/support/parity.rs) and enforced by test_parity_coverage_is_accurate,
# rather than left implicit here (ferritin-100.20).
#
# To add coverage: generate the fixture, un-ignore it below, and flip its
# PARITY_COVERAGE entry to Committed.
*.safetensors
!esm2_parity.safetensors
!amplify_parity.safetensors
# 125 KB: ProtT5's d_model is 1024, so four short sequences of F32 embeddings
# cost more than the ESM logit fixtures. Still small enough to commit, and it is
# the only thing checking a 1.2B-parameter port (ferritin-goh.5).
!prott5_parity.safetensors
# 4 KB: a 93-residue backbone plus its 93 structure token ids. The only thing
# checking the VQ-VAE structure encoder's numbers (ferritin-100.27).
!esm3_structure_parity.safetensors
# 60 KB: Ankh's d_model is 768, so four short sequences are smaller than the
# ProtT5 fixture. Also pins that Ankh's ids match the shared t5::tokenizer
# table (ferritin-goh.6).
!ankh_parity.safetensors
# ~1 KB: token ids only, no embeddings — ProstT5's output is discrete 3Di
# states, so the reference is the translation itself (ferritin-goh.6).
!prostt5_parity.safetensors
# ~80 KB each: (93, 21) log-probs and logits, plus the (93, 128) encoder node
# embeddings and the (93, K) neighbour list, so a regression can be localised to
# the featurizer, the encoder, or the decoder rather than only showing up as a
# different distribution. `enc_h_E` is deliberately NOT saved — at (93, K, 128)
# it is 2.3 MB (ferritin-100.11).
!proteinmpnn_parity.safetensors
!ligandmpnn_parity.safetensors
# 293 KB: (78, 960) F32 embeddings for one 76-residue sequence, BOS/EOS rows
# kept so a mismatch in special-token placement surfaces at position 0 or L+1
# rather than passing silently. Larger than the other embedding fixtures only
# because ESMC's d_model is 960 and no rows are stripped. This is the fixture
# that closed the last whole-family parity gap: Family::Esmc held three rows and
# nothing checked any of them (ferritin-100.33).
!esmc_parity.safetensors
